marble-device-support (1.0.0-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship a read-only NetworkManager profile for the China Telecom data
    connection (usr/lib/NetworkManager/system-connections/ct-data.nmconnection,
    apn ctlte). NM loads /usr/lib profiles since 1.36, so a fresh rootfs has
    cellular data as a working fallback route with zero manual setup. Ships
    with autoconnect disabled: enabling it while the modem is still coming up
    races ModemManager's initialization and trips the
    mm_iface_modem_count_bearers assertion (SIGABRT, upstream master bug).
    Bring data up after registration with 'nmcli con up ct-data'.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:55:00 +0800

marble-device-support (1.0.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Power the controller back on after programming the Bluetooth address in
    marble-mac-restore.sh. The script has to power hci0 down before
    'btmgmt public-addr' can take, and bluetoothd's AutoEnable only fires
    when the index is first added - which we already raced past with the
    power off - so after a clean boot the controller sat at Powered: no even
    though the address was correct. Explicit 'btmgmt power on' closes that
    race.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:10:00 +0800

marble-device-support (1.0.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the sensor chain, which never came up: hexagonrpcd_fw_dir pointed at
    /usr/share/qcom/ while firmware-xiaomi-marble installs the HexagonFS tree
    one level down, at /usr/share/qcom/hexagonfs/. With the wrong root the
    virtual FS resolves none of sensors/sns_reg.conf, sensors/registry/ or
    socinfo/, the SLPI's sensor_process asserts
    (sns_registry_sensor.c:321:SNS_RC_SUCCESS == rc) and remoteproc reports
    "crash detected in slpi"; hexagonrpcd then loses the FastRPC channel
    ("Broken pipe"), exits, and iio-sensor-proxy gives up with "'registry'
    sensor unavailable". Pointing -R at /usr/share/qcom/hexagonfs/ leaves the
    SLPI stable and hexagonrpcd running.
  * Ship 82-libssc-marble-sensors.rules: iio-sensor-proxy's own 80 rule tags
    the fastrpc nodes "ssc-light ssc-compass" only, so the accelerometer and
    proximity sensor the SLPI exposes are never claimed even though ssccli
    reads both. Appending "ssc-accel ssc-proximity" makes D-Bus report
    HasAccelerometer and HasProximity.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:05:00 +0800

marble-device-support (1.0.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge marble-wlan-mac.service and marble-bt-mac.service into one
    marble-mac-restore.service: both addresses come out of the same persist
    file (qca6490/wlan_mac.bin), so one unit mounts persist once, parses the
    MAC once and has a single boot-ordering point. WLAN half keeps loading
    ath11k_pci (still blacklisted in usr/lib/modprobe.d/marble-wlan.conf);
    Bluetooth half keeps pushing the derived address (WLAN MAC minus one on
    the last octet) through btmgmt, and now only warns on failure so a
    Bluetooth problem cannot fail the unit that Wi-Fi depends on.

